# Review routing. Read the caveat before turning this into a requirement.
#
# What this file does: names who should be asked to look at what. That is useful the moment
# there is more than one contributor, and it costs nothing before then.
#
# What it must not be allowed to do here: stand in for independent review. Every pull request
# on this repository is opened by `xnasusx` and carries commits authored by `RootCawsLLC`, and
# those are two accounts belonging to one person. Enabling "Require review from Code Owners" in
# branch protection would therefore make an approval from RootCawsLLC *satisfy* the requirement
# while being self-approval in substance — the configuration would read as fully controlled and
# the review would not have happened.
#
# That is the precise divergence this repository ships two checks to expose. `pr-review` reads
# the commit history rather than the settings, and it grades an approval from the commit's own
# author as a failure: "Only approval on #N is from the commit author (RootCawsLLC)". So the
# harness would catch it, correctly, and the repository would be running a control that exists
# to detect a hole its own configuration had institutionalised.
#
# Leave `require_code_owner_reviews` off until there is a second reviewer who is a second person.
# When there is, this file starts doing real work and the caveat can go.

*                       @RootCawsLLC

